    "title": "Angel Reese joins Atlanta Dream: What's her immediate impact?",
    "text": "April 6, 2026, 3:56 p.m. ETAngel Reese was traded to the Atlanta Dream from the Chicago Sky on April 6.Reese is projected to join a starting lineup that includes Jordin Canada, Allisha Gray, Rhyne Howard, and Brionna Jones.Following an April 6 trade, Angel Reese has moved on to the Atlanta Dream, sparking the question: how will she fit with the roster?The Dream opened WNBA free agency with a splash trade for the Chicago Sky forward as it looks to improve on a 30-14 regular-season record and a playoff appearance in 2025. Reese joins a team that seeks to compete for a championship now.What will the Dream starting lineup look like with Reese in it? How does she fit in head coach Karl Smesko's system? Will Reese have an immediate impact in Atlanta?Here's USA TODAY's analysis of Reese's fit within the Atlanta Dream roster.Atlanta Dream projected starting lineup with Angel Reese3 Jordin Canada | G 5-foot 615 Allisha Gray | G 6-foot-010 Rhyne Howard | G 6-foot-25 Angel Reese | F 6-foot-324 Brionna Jones | F 6-foot-3Angel Reese's fit within the Atlanta Dream starting lineupCanada, Gray and Jones are all unrestricted free agents, and Howard is a restricted free agent. However, the Dream are likely to bring all of the aforementioned players back to keep a consistent core as Atlanta continues its push to bring a championship home. Reese will likely replace restricted free agent and Sixth Player of the Year Naz Hillmon in the starting lineup.Hillmon, who had a career year last season, stepped into the lineup for 17 games after center Brittney Griner suffered injuries, and Atlanta had to shuffle its starting players. Hillmon was a glue player for Atlanta, often cleaning up the glass, saving possessions, providing lockdown defense and timely offense when asked. Reese will likely do the same, and the pair should complement each other well.The former Sky forward works well in the paint under the basket, scoring quickly. She also has an uncanny knack for rebounding, leading the league in rebounds per game the last two seasons. Reese, a former point guard, also brings facilitation skills to Atlanta, which will help keep the offense moving.Smesko helped Hillmon develop a 3-point shot last season and could do the same with Reese, who has been working to expand her offensive prowess. Smesko could also help Reese refine her shooting motion and her footwork in the paint, which should do wonders for her offensive production. She also will potentially have veterans around her, Hillmon, Jones and even Griner (if the team brings her back) to help her improve. It wouldn't be shocking to see Reese become an All-Star for a third consecutive season.",
